From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Olivier Li <olivierli@google.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 03:37:45 -0700
Subject: CacheStorage: Treat opaque responses as credentialed for CORP

Force `request_include_credentials = true` for opaque responses read
from CacheStorage, disabling the COEP:credentialless CORP exemption for
cached opaque responses.

The Fetch and Service Worker specs do not define how a cached opaque
response preserves or verifies the originating request's credentials
mode, making the COEP:credentialless CORP exemption unenforceable
across CacheStorage. Until the spec is updated, we keep the upstream
`external/wpt` tests unmodified and record the 16 resulting subtest
changes in Chromium-side `-expected.txt` baselines.

Bug: 499181801
Change-Id: Id775f824cefe6e00ee4ea74e68691bfe083a87f2
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8504130
Commit-Queue: Rakina Zata Amni <rakina@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Eriko Kurimoto <elkurin@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Rakina Zata Amni <rakina@chromium.org>
Auto-Submit: Olivier Li Shing Tat-Dupuis <olivierli@google.com>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1711147}

diff --git a/content/browser/cache_storage/cache_storage.proto b/content/browser/cache_storage/cache_storage.proto
index ae1c02b209102162d5a454cbc13ea9b2eac54be6..7f84f11fff41b11604173d6ccb7eeba1d8e6362c 100644
--- a/content/browser/cache_storage/cache_storage.proto
+++ b/content/browser/cache_storage/cache_storage.proto
@@ -79,6 +79,11 @@ message CacheResponse {
   optional string request_method = 14;
   optional int64 padding = 15;
   optional int64 side_data_padding = 16;
+  // Renderer-supplied via cache.put() and therefore NOT trustworthy: a
+  // compromised renderer can claim a credentialed response was
+  // credentialless. Read it through CreateResponse() in
+  // cache_storage_cache.cc, which sanitizes it for opaque responses, rather
+  // than consuming this field directly.
   optional bool request_include_credentials = 17;
   optional bool has_range_requested = 19;
 }
